17592186338543 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "90908b74-fc45-5e32-b466-62e0d10d8c44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186337593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338595 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ad3d3925-f645-5ca5-bd69-c443c9ab9ea2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338927 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338927 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71269" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338927 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338927 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $x=1$ and $y=-z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338927 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8dcce0be-d5f7-5cfa-b79c-7ffd73c0f53e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338927 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $x=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y=-z$ (or $y+z=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338943 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338943 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338943 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338943 #edb/ref 1071 "The intersection of the planes $x+2y+3z=0$ and $3x+2y+z+8=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338943 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2974487-1652-5f64-b7d4-0706a72b18a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338943 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives    \n\n$$\nx+2(0)+3z=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3z,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ and $x=-3z$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z+8 & =0 \\\\ 3(-3z)+2(0)+z+8 & =0 \\\\ -8z & =-8 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-3z=-3$ and $a=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+2y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,2,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x+2y+z+8=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,2,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,2,3⟩\\times ⟨3,2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-4i+8j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n\n$$\nb=-\\frac{1}{4}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨1,-2,1⟩.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-3+1=-2,$ and $b=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388020 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388020 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388020 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388020 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $2x=6$ and $z=1-y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388020 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c61ebc2f-8bbc-5c89-bcf3-6676fa54cd9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388020 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $2x=6$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=1-y$ (or $y+z=1$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388021 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8224c570-9b5e-580f-8450-ee7ed8cf16e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388022 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨2,-2,1⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388022 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388022 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9137657-ea64-55ac-a50c-776389fe269a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388023 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-2,1,2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388023 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388023 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ccb2d8a9-4b43-5c1d-a4f4-5266329e7446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388024 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,-2,2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388024 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388024 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dbb29629-4b1b-5406-ae1b-3f10adcfde85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388025 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-2,2,0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388025 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388025 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf5bcfcc-b800-5ca5-aba0-22a1220a9fbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388026 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨1,-2,2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388026 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388026 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9b00eaee-d865-5c36-ba00-8bc6c7e12db0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413738 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413738 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413738 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0adea858-c23c-564c-9506-9e4a60396c0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413739 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413739 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413739 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "22b5f065-43d8-5efe-9322-eca1974cc3d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413740 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413740 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413740 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6d9614ef-645c-5eb3-83fc-f33c2f35aca1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413741 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413741 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413741 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6dc4adca-656f-5e68-9890-f48be898ac6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413742 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413742 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413742 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f5604891-08a1-55fe-b657-ffce04ef2384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413743 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aef76bea-df64-529b-85e7-fa51fb7e165e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413744 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413744 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71465" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413744 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413744 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the two planes $x+y+z=0$ and $x+y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,1,0⟩.$\n- The planes intersect on a line.\n- The planes are coincident." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413744 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "abe7bafd-4069-5c23-9e34-e0cbd57e3732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413744 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x+y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,1,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x+y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\times ⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+j \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩\\ne ⟨1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
